\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The overall framework of our multi-modal knowledge transfer (MKT) model for open-vocabulary multi-label classification. Our MKT mainly consists of a vision and language pre-training (VLP) model and a vision transformer model. The VLP model aims to extract multi-modal knowledge of input image-text pairs, while vision transformer is used to extract semantic features of input images. Moreover, knowledge distillation is used to guarantee the consistency of image and its relevant label embeddings, along with prompt tuning to further update the label embeddings. (Best viewed in color.) }}{3}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overall_arch}{{2}{3}{The overall framework of our multi-modal knowledge transfer (MKT) model for open-vocabulary multi-label classification. Our MKT mainly consists of a vision and language pre-training (VLP) model and a vision transformer model. The VLP model aims to extract multi-modal knowledge of input image-text pairs, while vision transformer is used to extract semantic features of input images. Moreover, knowledge distillation is used to guarantee the consistency of image and its relevant label embeddings, along with prompt tuning to further update the label embeddings. (Best viewed in color.)}{figure.caption.3}{}}
